  howpublished = {International Conference on Big Data Computing and Communications (BigCom)},
  annotation = {中文辅助译名：TagVibra：突破基于 RFID 的振动传感的极限},
  abstract = {RFID-based mechanical vibration detection is considered a promising method for many Internet of Things (IoT) applications. However, existing methods are affected by ambient interference and leakage from the reader signature, which makes it difficult to obtain high-precision detection results. To overcome this limitation, this paper introduces TagVibra, a high-precision non-contact vibration sensing system based on RFID technology. By leveraging the nonlinear effect inside the tag and the modulation mechanism of RFID, TagVibra can achieve sub-millimeter level vibration detection accuracy. We implement TagVibra on our Universal Software Radio Peripheral (USRP) platform and evaluate its performance via experiments. The experimental results show that TagVibra can detect vibration with amplitude as low as 0.3mm, and the average estimation error below 0.7Hz when the vibration frequency is 100Hz.},
}

